{#-
  Shared guidance for the cvlr_kb RAG tools (cvlr_manual_search /
  cvlr_keyword_search / cvlr_get_section). One corpus, three manifests: the published
  Solana/CVLR manual, a generated reference for every public item of the CVLR crates,
  and idioms abstracted from real verification projects.
-#}
* `cvlr_manual_search(query, ...)` -- natural-language search across the CVLR corpus. Prefer it
  for conceptual questions ("how do I model a token account?", "when should a rule be
  parametric?").
* `cvlr_keyword_search(query, ...)` -- full-text search over the same corpus. Prefer it when you
  already know the identifier you want; it returns section titles to feed to `cvlr_get_section`.
* `cvlr_get_section(section_names)` -- fetch a section in full when you need its signature,
  examples or caveats.

The corpus is advice and reference. It is **not** the authority on what exists: it was written
against particular CVLR releases, and this project may resolve different ones. When the two
disagree, the crate source wins — see below.
